  "final_message": "**Status:** Reproduced\n\n**Expected**: With `<SubComponent>` inside `<BaseLayout>`, next to a `v-if` slot `<template>` for `BaseLayout`, both `#slot1` and `#_slot2` templates replace the fallback content in `SubComponent` (as in v3.5.13).\n\n**Actual**: On this revision (3.5.17), `#slot1` renders its template but `_slot2` renders its fallback content. The rendered HTML is `<div><p>named</p><b>slot1 works</b><i class=\"default\">DEFAULT _slot2</i></div>`.\n\n**Trigger**: All three of these are needed:\n- A slot name starting with `_` in `SubComponent`.\n- `SubComponent` is rendered inside `BaseLayout`'s default slot.\n- A conditional (`v-if`) slot `<template>` is a sibling of `SubComponent`.\n\nWithout the conditional sibling, `_slot2` renders correctly. That control is in the same spec and passes.\n\n**Run** (from the repo root, exits 1 while the bug is present):\n```\nnpx vitest run --project unit packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName.spec.ts\n```\n\n**Passes when**: The same spec, run against the published `vue@3.5.13` build, passes both tests. On the published `vue@3.5.14` it fails the same way, which matches the report's regression window.\n\n**Artifacts**: `packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName.spec.ts` (new file, which is the only change in the working tree). It has the failing reproduction plus the no-sibling control.\n\n**Caveats**:\n- The permission classifier blocked one of my two attempts to decode the playground links in the report. I did not retry that decode. I wrote the reproduction from the report's description of the trigger, with components built from runtime-compiled templates. It may not match the playground project line for line, but it shows the reported symptom.\n- No production code was changed.\n\n**Likely cause**: Slot names starting with `_` seem to be treated specially when slots are normalized or compiled. I did not trace this through the code.\n",
  "run_command": "npx vitest run --project unit packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName.spec.ts",
  "patch": "diff --git a/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName.spec.ts b/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName.spec.ts\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..9c752ab\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotName.spec.ts\n@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@\n+import { createApp } from '../src'\n+\n+// Reproduction for: \"Slot <template> not working when its name starts with an\n+// underscore (_) since v3.5.14\".\n+//\n+// Conditions from the report:\n+//  - SubComponent has slots whose names start with `_` (and a normal one)\n+//  - SubComponent is a sibling of a conditionally rendered (`v-if`) slot\n+//    <template> that is passed to BaseLayout (the slot need not exist there)\n+//  - SubComponent is rendered inside BaseLayout's default slot\n+describe('slot <template> with underscore-prefixed name', () => {\n+  const BaseLayout = {\n+    template: `<div><slot name=\"randomslotname\"></slot><slot></slot></div>`,\n+  }\n+\n+  const SubComponent = {\n+    template: `\n+      <slot name=\"slot1\"><i class=\"default\">DEFAULT slot1</i></slot>\n+      <slot name=\"_slot2\"><i class=\"default\">DEFAULT _slot2</i></slot>\n+    `,\n+  }\n+\n+  function mountApp(template: string) {\n+    const container = document.createElement('div')\n+    createApp({\n+      components: { BaseLayout, SubComponent },\n+      template,\n+      data: () => ({ cond: true }),\n+    }).mount(container)\n+    return container.innerHTML\n+  }\n+\n+  const withSibling = (cond: string) => `\n+    <BaseLayout>\n+      <template ${cond} #randomslotname><p>named</p></template>\n+      <SubComponent>\n+        <template #slot1><b>slot1 works</b></template>\n+        <template #_slot2><b>_slot2 works</b></template>\n+      </SubComponent>\n+    </BaseLayout>\n+  `\n+\n+  it('renders the provided #_slot2 content next to a conditional slot template (reported bug)', () => {\n+    const html = mountApp(withSibling('v-if=\"cond\"'))\n+    // expected: both provided templates replace the fallback content\n+    expect(html).toContain('slot1 works')\n+    expect(html).toContain('_slot2 works')\n+    expect(html).not.toContain('DEFAULT')\n+  })\n+\n+  it('control: same markup without the conditional sibling template', () => {\n+    const html = mountApp(withSibling(''))\n+    expect(html).toContain('slot1 works')\n+    expect(html).toContain('_slot2 works')\n+    expect(html).not.toContain('DEFAULT')\n+  })\n+})\n"
}
